Track 2: The Projectionist Who Bit The Lead
- Story & Context: Clara sits in the booth with a piece of metal screen-wire between her teeth, her tongue tasting of copper and industrial grime as she watches the empty screen. She is the keeper of the secret reel, a woman who knows the exact beat where the rhythm of the city aligns with the jump-cut of a missing narrative. She confesses to the shadows, "I taste the iron in every frames I swallow," knowing full well the machine will swallow her next.
