Track 3: The Majestic’s Last Burn
- Story & Context: The theater ignited in a flash of nitrate light, not from a match, but from the heat of the music reaching a frequency that the building could no longer contain. Locals say the ghosts of the projectionists still haunt the site, their instruments vibrating in the floorboards whenever the wind catches the debris in just the right rhythmic pattern. The myth persists as they chant, "the celluloid altar burns down to the final frame."
